	(text "SWD header (Nucleo ST-LINK/V2-1, connector CN4)\nSame pin order as CN4: straight wire-to-wire.\n+3V3 is reference only: power the FC from USB or PDB.\nSWDIO = PA13 / SWCLK = PA14, no resistors (internal pulls).\nNRST shared with the reset button.\nSWO = PB3 (pin 6): ITM trace output, MCU to ST-LINK only.\nCN4 pin 6 is marked \"Reserved\" in UM1724 Table 5."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 179.324 66.548 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.1588)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "2d209347-8e94-4500-9cb7-d493f875b3b0")
	)
	(text "NRST has an internal pull-up (~40kΩ), so it idles high\nwithout an external resistor.\nPressing SW1 pulls NRST to GND and resets the MCU.\nC15 (100nF) filters out noise-induced spurious resets."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.908 66.294 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.1588)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "48a9b46e-dd89-41e8-b739-b027b95ed9fd")
	)
	(text "References: AN4488 (sec. 3.1, Figure 4), DS8626 (sec. 6.3.17, Table 51, Figure 38)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 26.162 75.692 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
				(thickness 0.1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "49015ffb-8fd9-4cdc-b86c-af9c34714331")
	)
	(text "References: AN4488 (sec. 4.4.1, Table 6, Figure 12; sec. 9.3, Table 11), DS8626 (sec. 3.13)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 100.584 74.93 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "5a60c2ab-8947-453c-8df1-e8682ff22bde")
	)
	(text "C15 as close as possible to the NRST pin"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.908 73.406 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.3 1.3)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "7caebce2-b070-4acb-90f4-aeb68be05d3c")
	)
	(text "SWD DEBUG"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 178.816 57.658 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(thickness 0.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "9eb3c25c-dc7e-4c98-ba64-a865bd2d0ed9")
	)
	(text "R4 (10k) holds BOOT0 low, so the MCU boots from flash (firmware).\nTo flash over USB: hold SW2 and press reset. BOOT0 goes to 3V3\nand the MCU enters the bootloader (system memory).\nR16 (10k) holds BOOT1 (PB2) low. With BOOT0 = 1, BOOT1 = 0 selects\nsystem memory; BOOT1 = 1 would select SRAM boot.\nBoot pins must not float."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 100.33 67.818 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "de8a3594-258f-48ad-81d3-92378e49b5f4")
	)
